---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - TypingWire"
  description="Read the official Privacy Policy for TypingWire and the TypingWire Blog subdomain."
>
  <div class="prose-container policy-page">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      <span class="current">Privacy Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="header-tags">
      <span class="post-card-badge">LEGAL</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="display-lg">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: August 16, 2026</p>

    <hr class="section-divider" />

    <div class="article-content">
      <p>
        At <strong>TypingWire</strong> (accessible via <code>https://typingwire.in</code> and <code>https://blog.typingwire.in</code>), your privacy is one of our top priorities. This Privacy Policy document outlines the types of information that is collected and recorded by TypingWire and how we use it.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you visit our static blog portal (<code>blog.typingwire.in</code>), we do not require you to create an account or provide personal information to read articles. We may collect non-personal analytics data, such as:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Browser type and version</li>
        <li>Operating system (Windows, Mac, Linux, Android, iOS)</li>
        <li>Referring pages and time spent on articles</li>
        <li>Aggregated IP addresses (anonymized)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Cookies and Web Beacons</h2>
      <p>
        Like any other website, TypingWire uses standard cookies to store information including visitors' preferences and the pages on the website that the visitor accessed or visited. The information is used to optimize the users' experience by customizing our web page content based on visitors' browser type.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Third-Party Services and Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We may employ third-party analytics providers (such as Google Analytics or Cloudflare Analytics) to help us measure web traffic and usage trends. These tools collect information sent by your device including cookies and usage information.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Data Protection & Security</h2>
      <p>
        All communication with <code>blog.typingwire.in</code> is encrypted using industry-standard SSL (HTTPS). We do not sell, trade, or rent user personal identification information to others.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have additional questions or require more information about our Privacy Policy, do not hesitate to contact us at <a href="mailto:support@typingwire.in">support@typingwire.in</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy-page {
    padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 5rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--colors-muted-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--colors-primary);
  }

  .last-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--colors-muted-text);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .section-divider {
    border: 0;
    height: 1px;
    background-color: var(--colors-hairline);
    margin: 2rem 0 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
